        <p>IN CONCLUSION. I e4.n on::. ,ay that the greatest marvel of all is that Mr. Worsley has 'instituted a new Gt.:Anal Payment System, which he in&amp; igurate 1. Vi'orsley's off-r you all the 'Alvan- vantages of their :ow -0, ieei. Any ol ti:e bargains I have described may be porcha,,d at the prices advertised, and they will allow you to jay off by fitrininat linyments, making RA diff,retice whatever in the invoii e iifice, I cannot ccnclude my letter without recotnnu nding everyone to , visit Woreey's before Pur,l,S".g . a. b:s aumpettOrs try to imitate his style of business, but my expsTience teaches me that Worsley.nigiis sto:rel:io—Wor,ley i 6 I i era, the rest are nowhere o or,le:.*:, a:- open cyery day from 9to 7, and " the Pan:h on," being sOnost next, door to the Central tati,in, l'elanche,Lei ,ts i, ely easy ti rind. The sic Park, Junction. intd Bradshaw-street trams all going City- road way pass the door.</p>
