        <p>DRUNK AND BRAKING WINDOWS.—Kate Ann Jon;s, Ashton-street was charged with being (irunk and disorderly In A.shton-street on Satnrday nlht.. eh q was a!so ehared with breaking windows the props cry of Wcharcl Bond to the extent of 10,.—P.C..J0n-s proved the first case and a Mrs. Broderick the se-"ond. It was lo her house the windows were broken Defendant was fined ss. and costs and otclerkd to pay the damage. ASSAULT ON A PUBLICAN.—An Irish fa,rn labourer nand Patrick •,;haughnessy was charged with 'ring dronk and diSordeey in Bank-itreet on Saturday night and also with assaulting Michael Higgins at the same time and niaos. He pleaded gulity.—P.C. Barrett (31) pr.-ved the first oftenc-, and Mi hael Higgins, licensee of the Royal Arms said the (1.-fennant c-me in drunk and witness had to ei-ct hm Ile returned for his cap and struck witness in the eve cutting It —The magistrates said they could not allow p•iblicoris to be a•saulted when tryinlz to keep tb ir houses ord-r:y and would send defendant to kaul for one month with hard labor.</p>
        <p>DRUNK AND DISORDERLY,— For being guilty of drunken- ness Hnd disorderh conduct in Horsemarket-itreet on Sunday monining John France was fined ss. including coots.</p>
        <p>PICRING A MAN'S P OCEET.—Stephen Collins was charged with stealing fforn John M'Keown in this " HiAer Seven Stars "on Sunday night, 16.--11•Keown, the prnseentor an elderly man, said he and aritioner were both in the" Sewn Stars "at the same time. Witness w,s just go- tag out when p-isoner came to him and a,ke 1 him it he had any money and accompanied the question bv putting his hand Into witness's vest pocket and taking the shilling. When wit- ness tied to get it baek he threatened to " bate " him. He gave inforrnAion to the police and prioner visa atpreliendei. —PC. Corcor in proved the apprehension of prison(ir who said in answer to the charg " I know nowt, about it." A man named Mitchell said he saw prisoner take th money and he atte plait to pas it to witness.—Prisoner nho tpel 11 convictions against him was sent to gaol for one month's hard 'Meow.</p>
        <p>AMA ULT.—Jane Johnon, 40th appearance was tined 58. and costs for assanlting a woman nameA Sarah Ann Dicken- son on he 7th April.</p>
        <p>TUESDAY.—Before Mr. R. Garnett (in the chair) and Mr. E.</p>
