        <p>INTEMPERANCE —Mary Fitzgerald, a woman from Man- cheater, was fined ss. aid costs for b-ing drink am! ds- erdrlv In yst at ten minutes to six on Monday ight WiPst: Aaseur.T.--..fam‘ s ard wis eharged with assan'ting and heating his wife Bride, and ,•lso Margaret Kelly on the 19th April.—Defendant uilty —The dhief Constab'e said the eomnlaina-t was grantod a free warrant, on i•Tood ag,iin-t, her im-bind for ass nit. • She was accompanied by Margaret Kelly and both were mark e 4 owing prisnner's %dol.-rte. The case sary tha. on Sunday at one th • pri- soner came to hi, home flayhorBe-yari, and asked hi., wife for mr.ne 7 for drink. She slid she had none to g:ve him for that purpose. He at. once eommencel a savage and dastardly assault upon her. He struck her and knocked her d-avii and then dragged her by her bar. He knelt noon her in I erushrd her till she conld searc.,•ly breathe. Margaret Ke'lv had not appeare . and he thought. she was afraid of prisoner. —Mrs. Ward stibstantiatod.gr. Talbot's st,t/7mr•nt and said that Margaret Kelly wo,lld not coma because she till not want, to come between man and wife.— Petective-Sergeant Monaghan said wi-n he anprehensled defendant and told him the reason he said '' I will give her more when I come out.' He was un ,er the influence o drink —The Chairman said he th ;right it, was uafortunate tkit the law did n t admit of the use of the cat-of-nine tails in that case If it &amp;I he would warrant that h 3 would be sure to et it Defendant would have to go to gaol f r three month, hard labour.—on the up- pile tion of the c plainaot a separation order was granted her with ss. a week mainte ATICA.</p>
        <p>Titunsn.T.—Beiore Al lerman Sutton and Colonel Rid Att ATTEMPT Tr) RE-ENT,T,T MurlnV vertg handed over to the m Mary al.thorittes to tw dcat with on tlharl.fe of Dilating in the Militia at Orford when h had previously been digeharged from one et. gitnent for felony. BEGOING —qtenhen Birmingham a tramp, was eharced with begging in Bridgo-street on Wednesdayafter Clough proved the °i.e.—Prisoner. with an Moa of extenuat- ing the c ime toy making it appetr as a matter of noire..aid bob d been no mod down the country for 12 months doing this sort of thing your worships."—The Chief Cl.nstatOe : T) ow say a full contagion is good for the soul.—Prisoner was commit te for a month.</p>
