        <p>RUNCORN PETTY SESSIONS. MONDAT.—Before Sir Richard Brooke, Bart., and Mr. James Handley. STREET VOOTBALL.- For playing football in Brook-st.,John Critcbley and Alfred Plant, were ordered to pay the costs. ' ALLEGED WIFE DESERTION.—CharIes Johnson, 6. Picow- st., appeared to answer a summoss taken out by Elizabeth Johnson. his wife, for deserting ber and her two children. The defendint wis represented by Mr. Allen, who stated that the case had been before the court and afijourn'e,i in order to see if some arrangements could not be made. There were two children by a former husband, and defendant was willing as soon as he could 14,Lt work to contribute 2s. per week to his own child. Defendant had be).n ont of work six months, and as no means had been shown an order could not be made against her. --Conolainant wanted defendant to take the child as she could not get her own living.—The case was adjourned for a month t) give the parties an opportunity of effecting a settlement.</p>
