fting, she was committed ASSiZnP to prison for fnur month.. In August, 1.130 J, stealing velvet she got three months, and again stealing cashmere she was dismissed with a eau"t Prisoner had a most respectable husband, and be 0 Chief Constable) could say for him that he had been.v straightforward with the "police, as ,possible. and he fie sisted them in every v4v The 'articles as they 104 pawned ran from July 5 1895, to April, 1896-001' the whole of the time F had be nin Warrington. to The Chairman (Alderman Sutton) said the freque, of these thefts from the market rendered it meteor; te deal with each defendant so as to be a warning .4 others It seemed to be a very serious case indeed, f,"fi. to deal with it in any ther Vrti.V would be wrong.2drj snner would have to go to gaoffor three months' labour. rnaV</p>
